SECTION I. 
Introduction 
 
Text entry user interface is the essential part of human interaction access point to trigger the starting, operating, and controlling the processes of the potential system. However, with traditional computing devices, text entry user interfaces still have a bottleneck such as the chance of breakage or infection transfer when it is public usage. Currently, one of the promising approaches to solve this problem is a virtual keyboard. A virtual keyboard is where a full-size image of a QWERTY keyboard is projected onto any surface. Touching the image of any keys will generate the input to the system corresponding to a key's image. With a touchless virtual keyboard, there is no cleaning required, and they have no wires, buttons, or switches to maintain. Those benefit of the virtual keyboard is significant and, therefore, it brought a lot of research attentions into this application area. 
 
In order to provide a robust virtual keyboard, we need an effective hand typing recognition model. Recently, most hand gesture recognition methods focus on tracking hand pose estimation or detecting hand gestures [1] . The hand pose estimation is convenient to track click actions on the clicked region. However, this method is not suitable when the keyboard buttons are too small or there are nearby multiple buttons. In contrast, our framework can detect typing motions of two-hand fingers in the air which are similar to a regular typing on a keyboard. Therefore, our framework is much easier to use and implement in real-world applications. 
 
In addition to the hand typing recognition model, the data-preprocessing step is also important to enhance the performance. Existing works like a visual keyboard for smart TV in [3] and a virtual keyboard design in [4] proposed hand tracking and fingertip movement recognition methods using geometric features of the hand for data-preprocessing technique. In contrast, we use Motion History Image (MHI) [2] technique for feature extraction. The MHI is widely employed by various researches for action recognition, motion analysis and other related applications. The advantage of MHI is showing an object movement, clear shapes and removing the background, as shown in Figure 1 [2] . 
