A. Data Preprocessing 
 
To recognize the typing action, we need hand motion shapes on image sequences from a single RGB camera first. For this, we use the Background Subtraction Technique (BST), a widely used approach for detecting moving objects in video frames from static cameras. The main idea of the technique is detecting the moving objects from the difference between the current frame and a reference frame. We have tested several BST such as Gaussian Mixture-based Background, Foreground Segmentation Algorithm, and Bayesian segmentation. However, they could not show enough results. Then we have derived a BST for MHI by modifying existing BST. Our MHI has three following steps. 
 
First step. To convert the RGB image to greyscale image. The image sequence is obtained from the last frames of the camera as shown in Figure 4 . 
