B. Data Collection 
 
Data collection is one of the important parts of building a deep learning model. Since our method is different from the existing methods, there is no public dataset suitable for our model. Therefore, we develop a simple data collection tool to speed up our data collecting process. The tool collects image sequences for each class. Then image sequences were generated to get a single image of MHI. A screenshot of the data collection tool is shown in Figure 9 . 
 
Our dataset contains 5,180 data collected by 12 people. The data in the dataset is classified into 11 classes in terms of finger motions. There is one class for the negative case and other ten classes are for 10 fingers of the two hands. The negative case consists of random hand motions, expect touch actions, as shown in Figure 8 . 
