Conclusion 
 
In this paper, we present an efficient hand typing motion recognition system for Virtual Keyboard using a single RGB camera. The recognition part uses MHI for feature extraction and classify data using CNN. Our virtual keyboard runs smoothly when FPS is 25–30. 
 
In real-time testing, the best score is 92% in the experienced group. In the not experienced group, the score is 67%. The two scores were quite a difference because not experienced group first time type in the air and it needs more practice. Also, they understand to perform air typing quickly. It shows our framework is ready to be used for real world applications. As future work, we plan to add push clicking gesture in order to improve real-time performance and apply for mobile devices. 
 
